# The headers of the document: what the browser is told about the page and the files it loads. The Caddyfile imports this file
# inside the block that serves the web app, so they are sent with those files and with nothing else. `/api` and `/collab` are
# answered by the server, which sets its own (T7.2): the proxy does not add these to them, so the two never contradict each other.
#
# The shape of this file is a contract (ADR 0016): exactly one `header { … }` block, never a named snippet, with these values; T7.2
# keeps them all and replaces only the policy. `apps/server/test/deploy/caddy-fragment.test.ts` checks it with Caddy.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy of the page needs the hash of every inline script of `index.html`, which exists only after the web
# build. The `web-build` stage of the Dockerfile runs `apps/web/scripts/security-headers-caddy.ts` on the built page and on this
# file: the output is this file with the one `Content-Security-Policy` line replaced by the whole policy (the hashes,
# `frame-ancestors 'none'`, which works only as a header, and `connect-src` narrowed to this host), and the proxy image gets that
# output in its place. Every other line is kept as it is. The line below is what the file says in the repository, where there
# is no build to take hashes from.
header {
	# A browser that has seen the site over HTTPS keeps using HTTPS for a year, which is what makes the `Secure` session cookie
	# reliable. No `includeSubDomains` and no `preload`: this site cannot speak for the other names under its domain, and a
	# preload cannot be taken back.
	Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
	X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
	Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
	# The app needs none of the capabilities a page can ask for.
	Permissions-Policy "camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()"
	Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy "same-origin"
	# The page is never shown in a frame of another site. The generator writes the rest of the policy over this line.
	Content-Security-Policy "frame-ancestors 'none'"
	-Server
}
